A||||6||Formula||K&N works!
Z||000000||Formula||08-26-99||01:08 PM||||I bought the K&N air filter and put it in.  Before when I started my car it idled funny (dropped to 500 then bounced to 1000.....) and it stayed at 220 degrees F. Well, the filter made my car run as smooth as it can possibly run and the heat dropped to around 160. I didn't notice the 5 horses but I think its a good buy. Now you can even hear it rumbling underneath of the exhaust leak. I recommend it.
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||08-26-99||08:28 PM||||Formula, Iam with you. I have tried differant intake mods I have a K&N cone I think it helps you can hear the air being sucked up into the tube. The end of the cone is right at the side scoop opening.<p>What about a 100 cfm fan in the tube??
Z||000002||Cooter||08-26-99||09:08 PM||||maybe a 300 cfm fan would be better- reference to Terrybogin's post in the other k-n filter post.
Z||000003||lowCG||08-26-99||09:14 PM||||Water injection will do more than a fan.
Z||000004||FieroGT||08-27-99||01:17 PM||||A fan for what? If is in any way meant to pressurize the intake charge, you would be wasting your time. I participated in a discussion about this once, on the Turbo Grand Prix board. I don't have the physics formulae to back me up, but I do know that a fan placed inline with the intake would ultimately be more of an obstruction than anything else.<p> Does anyone recall the dyno tests by Herb Adams (circa 1986?) that indicated that there was no difference in horsepower running the Fiero 2.8 with all intake ducting completely removed. Open throttle body. Said that Pontiac engineers did their homework on the Fiero's intake; being that it posed virtually no restrictions despite the fact that it looks very restrictive. That's another reason I don't think that the K&N filter does much for the Fiero. Don't get me wrong, I have one in my GT. It was reasonably priced ($23) and I figured that it would be the last filter I'd ever buy for the car. I wouldn't want people to but it expecting to shave 1/2 second off their 1/4 mile times, because they'll be dissappointed. Just my $0.02.....
Z||000005||theogre||08-27-99||07:35 PM||||Formula, what did you change besides the filter. There is no way in hell a filter change would drop engine temp 60F.
Z||000006||Formula||08-27-99||07:48 PM||||I honestly only changed the filter and the temp dropped.  It did go back to idling funny when cold though.  Just a thought........ Would 89 octane instead of 93 octane affect the temp.... I doubt it but who knows?
